  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the best at 0.629 acc, while config_050 (scgpt variant) underperforms at 0.518 and costs more, confirming pca_n2000 is the superior RNA encoder. config_009 (image-only) at 0.332 confirms multimodal is essential. The remaining uncertainty is whether the fusion mechanism (concat vs weighted) meaningfully affects performance. This experiment tests weighted fusion as the sole change from the best config, directly clarifying whether learned channel weighting improves over simple concatenation. It is the best use of this slot because it is a minimal, single-variable perturbation of the top performer with expected cost similar to config_001 (~4.5 GPU hours, since weighted fusion is a lightweight learned scalar per modality rather than a new module), making it the cheapest informative step. A positive result opens a family of weighted-fusion configs to exploit; a null result lets us redirect budget toward aggregation (transformer) or image-encoder ablations without wasting a slot."
